The following releases have been created:

release 0.1 (2007-12-20)

        Initial version created.

release 0.2 (2008-05-09)

        Fixed bug #0002066. Now, the debug macros are silent if the
          configuriaton file does not exist. Additionally, the output logfile
          is opened only if a configuration file exists.
        Applied some source code reformatting.
        Added an extended macro DSTART_EXT which distinguishes between the
          function name that should be printed out in enter/exit messages,
          and a so-called activation name determining when to print a debug
          message.
        Added function ddestroy() freeing memory space allocated dynamically
          for output streams.

release 0.3 (2008-07-15)

        GCC 4.2.1 compatibility achieved.
        GCC 4.3.1 compatibility achieved.

release 0.4 (2008-08-10)

        Fixed a bug in dclose() related to the destruction of the ostream for
          cout.
        Added generic ICDInt number representation.

release 0.5 (2012-09-21)

        Improved build infrastructure such that compilation outside the source
          tree is supported.
        Removed directive 'using namespace std;' from header files in order to
          keep namespaces clean (Ticket #0003104).
        Added novel debug macro DDUMP() which dumps the current stack of
          function calls to cout.
        Shifted entire project to C++11 language standard.

release 1.0 (2017-02-16)

        Added I/O functions for colored error, warning, assertion and
          information messages.

release 1.1 (2021-11-23)

        Switched to 64-bit builds by default.
        Complete redesign of debug macros, featuring proper C++11 coding style,
          more efficient internal data structures using numeric hashes instead
          of strings, and including the proper documentation of all preprocessor
          macros, data structures, classes and helper functions.

